{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-explainer-about-daily-conversation-hobbies-and-what-people-talk-about-in-daily-life-com/audio/main-3fbcff65b41f.mp3","durationSec":176.088,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":7.88,"text":"What people talk about in daily life is often a weekend hobby, like NPB baseball in Japan or the Super Bowl in the USA."},{"start":9.18,"end":11.54,"text":"Small talk is short, polite conversation."},{"start":12.26,"end":14.36,"text":"It helps people feel friendly and comfortable."},{"start":15.06,"end":17.44,"text":"It is not a serious meeting or a business deal."},{"start":18,"end":22.6,"text":"Weather, weekend plans, food, hobbies, and sports are often safe topics."},{"start":23.02,"end":29.1,"text":"A simple lens can help us understand this talk: the topic, the local example, and the person’s own interest."},{"start":29.7,"end":32.54,"text":"Not everyone in one country likes the same things."},{"start":33.88,"end":36.42,"text":"Watching sport is a popular hobby in Japan."},{"start":37.28,"end":45.42,"text":"In a 2024 survey, 47.4% of adults watched NPB professional baseball on TV during the past year."},{"start":46.12,"end":51.36,"text":"People may talk about a weekend game or summer high school baseball at Koshien Stadium near Osaka."},{"start":52.3,"end":54.9,"text":"Ichiro Suzuki is another famous topic."},{"start":55.36,"end":62.46,"text":"He played for the Orix BlueWave and the Seattle Mariners, and he set an MLB record with 262 hits in 2004."},{"start":63.42,"end":67.26,"text":"Karaoke is singing with recorded music while reading words on a screen."},{"start":68.14,"end":72.34,"text":"Daisuke Inoue built coin karaoke machines in Kobe in 1971."},{"start":73.16,"end":75.08,"text":"The machines used 100 yen coins."},{"start":75.9,"end":81.58,"text":"Today, friends often rent a small private karaoke box by the hour after work or on a weekend."},{"start":82.26,"end":86,"text":"Some people also enjoy hitokara, which means singing karaoke alone."},{"start":86.3,"end":88.68,"text":"The same hobby can therefore be social or private."},{"start":88.68,"end":91.34,"text":"Daily talk in Japan also follows the seasons."},{"start":91.9,"end":99,"text":"In late March and early April, people may visit Ueno Park in Tokyo for hanami and picnic under its many cherry trees."},{"start":99.7,"end":102.9,"text":"Another weekend topic is an onsen trip."},{"start":103.56,"end":107.22,"text":"An onsen is a Japanese hot spring and the baths around it."},{"start":107.66,"end":112.42,"text":"Dogo Onsen in Matsuyama and Beppu Onsen in Oita are well-known places."},{"start":113.22,"end":117.64,"text":"These trips give people easy Monday topics about weather, food, and travel."},{"start":118.4,"end":122.82,"text":"In Germany, 57% of people say they are interested in watching football."},{"start":123.52,"end":127.32,"text":"Monday talk may be about a Bundesliga match or FC Bayern Munich."},{"start":128.22,"end":134.66,"text":"Active hobbies are also important: 42% of German adults rode a bicycle at least once in 2020."},{"start":135.58,"end":139.16,"text":"In Switzerland, people often discuss weekend hikes in the Alps."},{"start":140,"end":146.76,"text":"The country has more than 65,000 kilometres of marked trails, with yellow Wanderweg signs that show walking time."},{"start":146.76,"end":154.18,"text":"In Spain, cafe or work talk may follow El Clasico, the football match between Real Madrid and FC Barcelona."},{"start":155.1,"end":161,"text":"In the USA, American football is the favourite sport to watch for about 41% of adults."},{"start":161,"end":167.1,"text":"Families often watch NFL games during Thanksgiving weekend, and the Super Bowl is another major topic."},{"start":167.7,"end":171.34,"text":"Like NPB talk in Japan, these games offer shared stories."},{"start":172.02,"end":175.48,"text":"However, personal interest is always more important than nationality."}],"words":[{"text":"What","st